   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Good morning,<br><br>I am trying to fit a bifactor model where the general factor (G) is the main focus and the specific factors (S1/S2) are viewed as nuisance factors. Previous examples I found do not seem to use the WLSMV estimator. Is there a reason for why the (ordinal) data should not be considered ordered in this case?<br><br>If I fit a model with the code below it will not converge unless I restrict at least one item (e.g., S1 =~ 0*i1 + i2 + i3 + i4 + i5 + i6 + i7). I have a pretty large sample (~20,000). Does anyone have an idea of why this happens, and how the restriction of this item affects the interpretation of the results?<br><br>mod &lt;- &#39;<br>G =~ i1 + i2 + i3 + i4 + i5 + i6 + i7 + i8 + i9 + i10 + i11 + i12 + i13 + i14<br>S1 =~ i1 + i2 + i3 + i4 + i5 + i6 + i7<br>S2 =~  i8 + i9 + i10 + i11 + i12 + i13 + i14<br>&#39;<br><br>fit &lt;- cfa(model=mod, data=data,<br>           ordered=names(data),<br>           estimator=&quot;WLSMV&quot;,<br>           parameterization=&#39;theta&#39;,<br>           se=&quot;robust.sem&quot;,<br>           <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426030199000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ULuQycVXIwpnd-T34YX--\">std.lv</a>=T,<br>           orthogonal=T<br>          )<br><br><br>Best,<br>Rico<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "3ZtL8MnDDAAJ",
   "from": "kma...@aol.com",
   "author": "ad188126f9138663",
   "date": "2018-02-23T03:48:16Z",
   "subject": "Re: Bifactor model with WLSMV",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Rico,<br>The issue appears to be sample specific.  Your model ran as expected for me using simulated data.  Perhaps the parameter estimate covariance matrix would shed some light?<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">lavInspect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> what</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;vcov&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br>Here is my test run:<br><br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>simMod </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>G =~ .4*i1 + .4*i2 + .4*i3 + .4*i4 + .4*i5 + .4*i6 + .4*i7 + .4*i8 + .4*i9 + .4*i10 + .4*i11 + .4*i12 + .4*i13 +<br>.4*i14<br>S1 =~ .4*i1 + .4*i2 + .4*i3 + .4*i4 + .4*i5 + .4*i6 + .4*i7<br>S2 =~ .4*i8 + .4*i9 + .4*i10 + .4*i11 + .4*i12 + .4*i13 + .4*i14<br>G ~~ 1*G<br>S1 ~~ 1*S1<br>S2 ~~ 1*S2<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>myDat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> simulateData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">simMod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nobs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>myBreaks </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>myDatCat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myDat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> MARGIN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FUN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">findInterval</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> vec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myBreaks</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myDatCat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>mod </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>G =~ i1 + i2 + i3 + i4 + i5 + i6 + i7 + i8 + i9 + i10 + i11 + i12 + i13 +<br>i14<br>S1 =~ i1 + i2 + i3 + i4 + i5 + i6 + i7<br>S2 =~ i8 + i9 + i10 + i11 + i12 + i13 + i14<br>&#39;</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> <br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cfa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myDatCat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span></div></code></div></div>"
